 Type 1 as an iterative stack-based traversal with pruning using the segment tree as described.\n- Type 3 queries simply check the value at tin[v] (1 => white, 0 => black).\nThis approach yields acceptable performance under the problem constraints, as updates via the segment tree are O(log n) and the Type 1 traversal is pruned by the presence of whites in subtrees. It avoids deep recursion by using an explicit stack for both the Euler tour and the Type 1 traversal.\n",
